  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, wonders aloud whether in the 1950s the US government had a program that handed out material recovered from crashed unknown craft to research centres. He has in mind FFRDCs, which are private research labs funded by the federal government. He suggests those materials may have sped up and inspired new technology, and he points to a former Army officer, Philip Corso, and an online researcher known as UAPGerb, as sources for the idea. If true, some modern inventions would trace back to recovered craft."
